<title>FINLAND: ATRIA SEES TOUGHER COMPETITION IN 1997.</title>
<headline>ATRIA SEES TOUGHER COMPETITION IN 1997.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish meat processing group Atria Oy said on Tuesday it expected competition to intensify this year, but group sales in the retail market would rise.</p>
<p>&quot;Domestic competition is increasing further as European meat prices fall, and will ... make it more difficult to make profits,&quot; it said in a statement with its 1996 results.</p>
<p>&quot;Atria Oy expects to increase its meat purchases clearly this year and also to boost retail market sales,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Its profit before extraordinary items rose to 74 million markka in 1996 from 67 million in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242</p>
